 ## Background
-The Residency-Octree Update method was introduced in the context of scalable web-based volume rendering of large biomedicine datasets. It was designed to efficiently manage the residency of volume bricks in a GPU cache while maintaining a hierarchical octree structure for culling. The method builds on earlier work in spatial culling and LRU cache eviction [S1, unofficial]. Dynamic Octree Generation was introduced in the context of Mega-NeRF for scalable construction of large-scale NeRFs. It addresses the challenge of managing octree size in memory-constrained environments by dynamically adjusting the tree based on rendering visibility [S2].
